# Definition of done

Apply this before saying a piece of work is finished.

- [ ] Acceptance criteria are demonstrably met, not merely implemented.
- [ ] It runs end to end and can be demoed. Code complete without integrated behaviour is not
      done. Verify the caller actually reaches the new code rather than assuming the wiring.
- [ ] The happy path and the expected failure path both have tests.
- [ ] No secret appears in code, logs, fixtures or responses.
- [ ] Errors are handled intentionally. No bare catch, no silent swallow, no hang without a
      timeout or a surfaced message.
- [ ] Database changes include a migration.
- [ ] Changed API contracts are documented.
- [ ] New or changed reusable frontend components have Storybook stories.
- [ ] Logs and identifiers are sufficient to diagnose a failure in production.
- [ ] Lint, formatting and type checks pass.
- [ ] The change is small enough to review and demo in one sitting.

## Before you claim it works

Start the app and exercise the path a user takes. Do not infer that a feature works from the
code reading correctly. In this repo the dashboard component was written correctly, the API
returned correct data, and the two never spoke to each other, which no amount of reading the
component would have revealed.
